# Settings screen

<p class="lede">
<code>turn-alerts</code> logs a line when an agent turn ends, for failed turns only or for every turn. The choice
lives in a settings screen in the app, and the server reads it on every turn.
</p>

<h2 id="schema">One schema for both sides</h2>

A settings document is defined once in `shared/` and stored per Paseo host. Defaults for every field make `{}` a
complete document, so a fresh install reads as valid settings.

<SourceFile path="docs-site/recipes/settings/shared/preferences.ts" />

<h2 id="server">The server reads them</h2>

`registerSettings` returns a handle: `read()` gives the current document, `subscribe` reports saves. The hook reads
on every turn, so a change applies to the next turn without a reload.

<SourceFile path="docs-site/recipes/settings/index.server.ts" />

<h2 id="screen">The screen</h2>

`useSettings` goes through `loading`, then `ready` or an error state with a reset action. A save sends the whole
document with the revision it was read at, so a save from another client in between is rejected instead of
silently overwritten. The settings components come from `@getpaseo/plugin/client/ui` and follow the app's theme.

<SourceFile path="docs-site/recipes/settings/client/alerts-screen.tsx" />

The client registers the screen and a Command Center item that opens it:

<SourceFile path="docs-site/recipes/settings/index.client.tsx" />

<h2 id="run">Run it</h2>

```sh
npx ppd install path/to/recipes/settings
npx ppd web --viewport 390x844 --command "Turn alert settings" --shot out/settings.png
```

```text
installing path/to/recipes/settings as turn-alerts into http://127.0.0.1:7800
turn-alerts: running (installed)
client: passes the app's registration rules
...
screenshot: ~/code/my-plugin/out/settings.png
console errors: none
plugin evaluation errors: none
```

<Shot
  src="/shots/settings-screen-phone.png"
  alt="The Turn alerts settings screen in the compact layout: a switch 'Log an alert when a turn ends', on, and a select 'Which turns' set to 'Failed or canceled'."
  width={700}
  height={526}
  narrow
  caption="The screen at 390x844, cropped."
/>

Click the switch by its label, and the server's subscription logs the saved document:

```sh
npx ppd web --command "Turn alert settings" --click "Log an alert when a turn ends"
npx ppd paseo -- plugin logs turn-alerts
```

```text
2026-10-18T08:20:31.677Z  stdout    alert settings saved: {"enabled":false,"turns":"failed"}
```

Switch it back on, run a failing fake agent turn (with `--fake-agent` on the daemon), and the hook logs the alert:

```sh
npx ppd web --command "Turn alert settings" --click "Log an alert when a turn ends"
mkdir -p /tmp/ws
npx ppd paseo -- run --provider fake-agent --cwd /tmp/ws '{"steps":[{"write":{"path":"b.txt","content":"b"}},{"fail":"boom"}]}'
npx ppd paseo -- plugin logs turn-alerts
```

```text
2026-10-18T08:25:00.582Z  stdout    alert: turn failed for agent a812c7be-1ab0-4dc2-80e5-15ec4125766a
```

<Callout kind="info" title="In ppd check">

`ppd check` evaluates the server with a settings handle that reads as the schema defaults and never reports a save,
so `read` and `subscribe` work during the check.

</Callout>
